Akana to Apigee Core Migration Tool – Low Level Design & Technology Evaluation

Design a migration utility to support Akana to Apigee API migration by analysing Akana API configurations, proxies, and OAS definitions, and defining how these map to equivalent Apigee API proxies. This story focuses on producing a low-level design and finalising the implementation language choice between Go and JavaScript.


Acceptance Criteri

A low-level design (LLD) is created for the Akana to Apigee migration utility.
The design explains how Akana API configuration, proxy definitions, and OAS will be extracted.
Mapping rules between Akana constructs and Apigee proxy components are clearly documented.
The approach for creating Apigee API proxies using Apigee management APIs is defined.
Limitations, gaps, or unsupported Akana features are identified and documented.
A comparison between Go and JavaScript (Node.js) is performed against agreed criteria.
A single programming language is recommended with clear justification.
The LLD and technology recommendation are reviewed and approved by architecture/engineering stakeholders.


Explore available tools, technologies, and migration approaches to support Akana to Apigee API migration, and define a high‑level migration strategy covering tooling options, automation feasibility, risks, and recommended approach.

Acceptance Criteria

Existing tools and utilities (vendor‑provided or open source) for Akana and Apigee migration are identified and reviewed.
Technology options for API migration automation are analysed at a high level.
Migration strategy options (manual, semi‑automated, fully automated) are documented with pros and cons.
Key risks, constraints, and dependencies for Akana to Apigee migration are identified.
A recommended migration approach and tooling strategy is proposed.
Findings are documented and reviewed with relevant stakeholders.
